    dict(key='11-act-2-figure', kind='figure', title='The installed version, and where each advisory is fixed',
         body='version_line',
         narration='Second demo: scanning the bill. [[slnc 400]] Along the bottom, versions of log4j, in order. [[slnc 300]] The amber one, two point fourteen point one, is the version in the image. [[slnc 300]] The green ones are where the advisories are fixed. [[slnc 700]] Above, the three advisories grype found. [[slnc 300]] C V E twenty twenty one, four four two two eight is log4 shell: critical, fixed in two point fifteen. [[slnc 300]] The next critical one is fixed in two point sixteen. [[slnc 300]] And a high one is fixed in two point seventeen. [[slnc 700]] Each bar runs from the installed version to the fix. [[slnc 300]] The installed version is below every fix, so all three advisories match. [[slnc 300]] And scanning the bill alone, without the image, finds the same ones.'),
    dict(key='12-act-2-1', kind='console', title='Act Two — Scanning it against known advisories',
         body='TWO. Scanning it against known advisories.\n  THE SCAN (the input):\n    command   grype shop-sbom:2.14.1 -o json\n    database  advisories, built within 7 days: yes\n  THE CRITICAL AND HIGH ADVISORIES IN log4j (the result):\n    CRITICAL  CVE-2021-44228  fixed in 2.15.0\n    CRITICAL  CVE-2021-45046  fixed in 2.16.0\n    HIGH      CVE-2021-45105  fixed in 2.17.0\n  HOW ONE MATCH IS MADE (CVE-2021-44228):\n    the bill says  log4j-core 2.14.1\n    the advisory   fixed in 2.15.0\n    compared       2.14.1 < 2.15.0: yes, so it matches',
         narration='The input: the grype command, and a database built within seven days. [[slnc 400]] The result: two critical advisories and one high in log4j, each with its fix. [[slnc 500]] How one match is made: two point fourteen point one is below two point fifteen, so it matches.'),
